>> title: Cinnamon Pasta
>> servings: 5
>> source: https://www.mccormick.com/blogs/recipes/greek-skillet

> This is called "Greek Skillet" but I call it cinnamon pasta ¯\_(ツ)_/¯ .

Cook @ground beef{1%lb} and @onion{0.5}(chopped) in a large #skillet{} on medium-high heat until beef is no longer pink, stirring occasionally. Drain fat. 

Add @oregano leaves{2%tsp}, @cinnamon{1%tsp} and @garlic powder{0.5%tsp}; mix well.

Stir in @beef broth{1%14.5oz can}, @diced tomatoes{1%14.5oz can}(undrained) and @tomato paste{2%tbsp}. Bring to boil. 

Stir in @penne pasta{1.5%cups}. Reduce heat to medium; cover and cook ~{10%minutes} or until pasta is nearly tender. 

Stir in @broccoli{1%cup}(florets) and @feta cheese{0.75%cup}(crumbled), reserving 1/4 cup for garnish. Cover. Cook ~{5%minutes} longer or until pasta is tender.

Sprinkle with remaining @feta cheese{0.25%cup}. Cover and let stand ~{5%minutes}.